    <string name="pdf_limits_help">Share a photo or screenshot to recognize and read its text. Automatic layout is the default for pictures. Try Scattered text / signs for isolated labels or Text block for dense screenshots. Images are resized before OCR to limit memory use. PDFs are read in page order. Scanned pages use on-device OCR (English and Persian included). Automatic first recognizes each page with both models, then chooses Farsi or English from the majority script for a second pass. Short or blurry text can be misidentified. Choose English + Persian for pages containing both languages. OCR resolution: 800–4000 pixels (default 2400); higher uses more memory and time. OCR can make mistakes. File size: 1–1024 MB (default 200). Text: 10,000–20,000,000 characters (default 2,000,000).</string>
